    <edge source="UV Radiation" target="Basal Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">UV Radiation is a primary cause of Basal Cell Skin Cancer, as it damages DNA in basal cells, leading to uncontrolled growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">causal relationship, carcinogenic exposure</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Treatment" target="Basal Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Treatment involves medical interventions like surgery and radiation therapy to cure or manage Basal Cell Skin Cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical intervention, disease management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Risk Factors" target="Basal Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Risk Factors such as UV exposure and fair skin increase the likelihood of developing Basal Cell Skin Cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">etiologic factors, disease predisposition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Recurrence" target="Basal Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Recurrence refers to the potential return of Basal Cell Skin Cancer after treatment, requiring ongoing monitoring and follow-up.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease progression, post-treatment surveillance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Epidermis" target="Basal Cell Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Basal Cell Skin Cancer originates in the Epidermis, specifically in the basal cells that divide to form new skin cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical origin, cellular pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
