    <edge source="Dermis" target="Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Skin Cancer often occurs in the Epidermis, but some types can extend into the Dermis, though basal cell skin cancer rarely involves the Dermis.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical spread, tissue involvement</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hypodermis" target="Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Skin Cancer primarily affects the Epidermis and Dermis, with rare cases extending to the Hypodermis, though this is uncommon for basal cell skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">tissue depth, cancer progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Squamous Cells" target="Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Squamous Cells are a type of skin cell that can develop into squamous cell carcinoma, a different subtype of skin cancer, distinct from basal cell skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular differentiation, cancer subtypes</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Melanocytes" target="Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Melanocytes produce melanin, which protects against UV radiation, but their dysfunction can contribute to melanoma, a separate type of skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">pigmentation, cancer subtypes</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Squamous Cell Skin Cancer" target="Skin Cancer">
      <data key="d4">34.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Squamous cell skin cancer is a specific subtype of skin cancer that is frequently managed with surgical excision, Mohs procedures, or radiation therapy, depending on tumor depth and location.&lt;SEP&gt;Squamous cell skin cancer is a specific type of skin cancer classified under the broader category of skin cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer subtypes, treatment modalities&lt;SEP&gt;classification, medical categorization</data>
