    <edge source="shave excision" target="low-risk">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Shave excision is commonly used for low-risk CSCC, removing superficial tumors while preserving surrounding healthy tissue.</data>
      <data key="d6">surface removal, tissue preservation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="standard surgical excision" target="high-risk">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Standard surgical excision is used for high-risk CSCC, ensuring wide margins to reduce the risk of recurrence or metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d6">margin control, recurrence prevention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="radiation therapy" target="high-risk">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radiation therapy is an alternative or adjunct to surgery for high-risk CSCC when complete excision is not feasible, targeting residual cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">radiation oncology, treatment adjunct</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="lymphovascular invasion" target="high-risk">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphovascular invasion is a key indicator of high-risk CSCC, as it signifies cancer cells have spread beyond the primary tumor, increasing metastatic potential.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastasis risk, tumor spread</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="platinum-based chemotherapy" target="very high-risk">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Platinum-based chemotherapy is used in combination with radiation for very high-risk CSCC to address systemic cancer spread and resistant tumors.</data>
      <data key="d6">systemic treatment, chemotherapy synergy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="immunotherapy with an immune checkpoint inhibitor" target="very high-risk">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Immunotherapy with immune checkpoint inhibitors is preferred for very high-risk CSC, enhancing the immune system's ability to combat advanced cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">immunotherapy, advanced oncology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="lymphovascular invasion" target="very high-risk">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphovascular invasion is strongly associated with very high-risk CSCC, necessitating aggressive treatment strategies to prevent distant metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastatic potential, treatment escalation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="endocrine tests" target="radiation therapy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
