    </edge>
    <edge source="Anaplastic Thyroid Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is an intensive treatment approach for anaplastic thyroid cancer, though it often requires additional therapies due to the cancer's aggressiveness.</data>
      <data key="d6">aggressive treatment, surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyroid hormone replacement therapy is often used post-surgery for patients who have undergone total thyroidectomy, regardless of cancer type.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-operative care, hormone regulation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroidectomy" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyroidectomy is a type of Surgery used to remove the thyroid gland, categorized as either Total Thyroidectomy or Lobectomy depending on the cancer's severity.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, medical treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">1.0</data>
      <data key="d5">treatment-for</data>
      <data key="d6">Surgery is a treatment option for localized Thyroid Cancer.</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Glioma" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is a primary treatment modality for gliomas, aiming to remove as much of the tumor as possible to reduce symptoms and improve outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment modality, medical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TURBT" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">TURBT is a specific type of surgical procedure used for treating early-stage bladder cancer, highlighting its role within the broader category of surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;TURBT is a specific type of surgical procedure used to treat non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, establishing its relationship to the broader category of surgery.</data>
      <data key="d6">procedural subset, surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Treatment Options" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is a primary treatment category that includes procedures like TURBT and radical cystectomy, which are critical for managing bladder cancer at various stages.</data>
      <data key="d6">interventional approach, treatment modality</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="Squamous Cell Carcinoma (CSCC)">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NCCN provides guidelines for managing and monitoring squamous cell carcinoma, including recommended skin exam frequencies and follow-up protocols.</data>
