      <data key="d5">Secondhand smoke increases the risk of NSCLC by exposing individuals to harmful chemicals without direct smoking.</data>
      <data key="d6">risk factor, environmental exposure</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blast Phase CML" target="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphoblasts are immature lymphoid cells that contribute to blast phase CML, a more aggressive form of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell differentiation, disease progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AML" target="Myeloblasts">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AML originates from abnormal myeloblasts, which are immature white blood cells that fail to mature properly and proliferate uncontrollably.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer origin, cell dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neuroendocrine Tumors" target="Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Neuroendocrine tumors are a specific type of lung carcinoma, often distinct from NSCLC in clinical and molecular features.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer subtypes, molecular biology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Airways" target="Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lung cancer originates from cells lining the airways, including bronchi, bronchioli, and alveoli, and affects respiratory function.</data>
      <data key="d6">pathophysiology, disease origin</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Carcinoma" target="Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lung cancer is a type of carcinoma, originating from epithelial cells and classified as a carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer classification, tumor types</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thoracic Surgeon" target="Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
