    <edge source="NCCN" target="Hodgkin lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NCCN provides patient guidelines and educational resources for understanding and managing Hodgkin lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">health information, medical resources</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="lymphatic system" target="Hodgkin lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hodgkin lymphoma is a malignancy that originates within the lymphatic system, involving abnormal growth of lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical condition, anatomical system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Reed-Sternberg cells" target="Classic Hodgkin lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Classic Hodgkin lymphoma is defined by the presence of Reed-Sternberg cells, which are diagnostic markers for this subtype.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic markers, cancer subtypes</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="popcorn-shaped cells" target="Nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma is characterized by popcorn-shaped cells, which are distinct from Reed-Sternberg cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer subtypes, cellular markers</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Guide T = Tumor" target="Bile Duct Cancer Stages">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Guide T = Tumor provides staging criteria for bile duct cancer, which are directly related to the stages described in Bile Duct Cancer Stages."|&gt;"staging criteria, cancer progression&lt;SEP&gt;The Guide T = Tumor provides the staging criteria for bile duct cancer, linking tumor size and spread to clinical outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d6">9&lt;SEP&gt;cancer staging, tumor progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma (NHL)" target="Follicular Lymphoma (FL)">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follicular Lymphoma (FL) is a specific subtype of Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma (NHL), classified based on B cell abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Follicular Lymphoma (FL) is a specific subtype of Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma (NHL), classified based on B cell abnormalities."|&gt;"subclassification, lymphoma types</data>
      <data key="d6">10&lt;SEP&gt;subclassification, lymphoma types</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Germinal Centers" target="Follicular Lymphoma (FL)">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follicular Lymphoma (FL) originates from abnormal proliferation in germinal centers, where B cells undergo mutations and form tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Follicular Lymphoma (FL) originates from abnormal proliferation in germinal centers, where B cells undergo mutations and form tumors."|&gt;"pathogenesis, lymphoma development</data>
      <data key="d6">9&lt;SEP&gt;pathogenesis, lymphoma development</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Centroblasts" target="Follicular Lymphoma (FL)">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Centroblasts, which are large B cells in germinal centers, contribute to the formation of follicular lymphoma through uncontrolled proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Centroblasts, which are large B cells in germinal centers, contribute to the formation of follicular lymphoma through uncontrolled proliferation."|&gt;"cell proliferation, tumor formation</data>
      <data key="d6">8&lt;SEP&gt;cell proliferation, tumor formation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Centrocytes" target="Germinal Centers">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Centrocytes are smaller B cells in the light zone of germinal centers, playing a role in the maturation and regulation of lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Centrocytes are smaller B cells in the light zone of germinal centers, playing a role in the maturation and regulation of lymphocytes."|&gt;"cell differentiation, immune regulation</data>
      <data key="d6">7&lt;SEP&gt;cell differentiation, immune regulation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="B cells" target="Centrocytes">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Centrocytes are smaller B cells in the light zone of germinal centers, playing a role in the maturation and regulation of lymphocytes."|&gt;"cell differentiation, immune regulation</data>
      <data key="d6">7</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="B cells" target="Centroblasts">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Centroblasts are larger B cells in the dark zone of germinal centers that divide rapidly and contribute to the formation of follicular lymphoma."|&gt;"cell differentiation, tumor formation</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphocytes" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Lymphatic System is a network of tissues and organs that includes lymphocytes, which are white blood cells critical for immune responses."|&gt;"immune system components, cellular function</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Marrow" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone Marrow is a component of the Lymphatic System where lymphocytes originate and mature."|&gt;"system components, cellular origin</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Spleen" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Spleen is a component of the Lymphatic System that filters blood and removes foreign material, including bacteria and cancer cells."|&gt;"system components, immune function</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thymus" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thymus is a component of the Lymphatic System that plays a role in the maturation of T cells."|&gt;"system components, immune development</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphatic Vessels" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphatic Vessels are components of the Lymphatic System that transport lymph throughout the body."|&gt;"system components, fluid transport</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prostate Cancer" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Prostate cancer can spread through the lymphatic system to distant lymph nodes, facilitating metastasis and disease progression.</data>
      <data key="d6">metastasis, immune system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Axillary Lymph Nodes (ALNs)" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Axillary lymph nodes are part of the lymphatic system and are common sites for breast cancer metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d6">lymphatic spread, metastasis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Anatomy" target="Lymphatic System">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Breast anatomy includes the lymphatic system, which plays a role in cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomy, metastasis pathway</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="B cells" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">B cells are a type of lymphocyte that produce antibodies to fight infections and are involved in the development of follicular lymphoma."|&gt;"cell types, immune function</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="T cells" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">T cells are a type of lymphocyte that directly attack infected cells and play a role in immune responses."|&gt;"cell types, immune responses</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Natural Killer (NK) cells" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Natural Killer (NK) cells are a type of lymphocyte that can recognize and destroy infected or cancerous cells without prior activation."|&gt;"cell types, immune defense</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="White Blood Cells" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphocytes are a subset of white blood cells specialized in immune responses, including antibody production (B cells) and direct pathogen elimination (T cells).&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are a subset of white blood cells that specifically play roles in immune responses, including antibody production and direct pathogen elimination.</data>
      <data key="d6">immune system, cell classification</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">ALL originates in lymphoid progenitor cells, which develop into lymphocytes, and is characterized by the overproduction of immature lymphoblasts.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer origin, cell proliferation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">ALL primarily affects lymphocytes, with abnormal lymphoblasts proliferating in the bone marrow and lymphatic system.</data>
      <data key="d6">immune system, cancer pathology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphocytes are a component of blood, playing a critical role in immune function and cancer pathology.</data>
      <data key="d6">blood composition, immune system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphatic system" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The lymphatic system is the environment where lymphocytes circulate and function, as it includes lymph nodes, vessels, and organs that support immune responses.</data>
      <data key="d6">immune system, lymphocyte function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL)" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (N3) arises from the uncontrolled growth of abnormal lymphocytes, which are white blood cells critical to immune defense.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) arises from the uncontrolled growth of abnormal lymphocytes, which are white blood cells critical to immune defense.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer origin, immune system dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Stem Cells" target="Bone Marrow">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow is the primary site where blood stem cells are generated and differentiate into all blood cell types.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell differentiation, tissue regeneration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Myeloid Leukemia" target="Bone Marrow">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AML originates in bone marrow, where abnormal myeloblasts accumulate, impairing the production of healthy blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cancer origin</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood" target="Bone Marrow">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow produces blood cells, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, which are essential for bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, tissue function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hematopoietic Stem Cells" target="Bone Marrow">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow contains hematopoietic stem cells, which are the precursor cells responsible for generating all types of blood cells through differentiation.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell production, tissue function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia" target="Bone Marrow">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">ALL originates in the bone marrow, where lymphoid progenitor cells develop into abnormal lymphoblasts.</data>
      <data key="d6">hematopoiesis, cancer origin</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphatic system" target="Spleen">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The spleen is a critical organ of the lymphatic system, filtering blood and supporting immune responses.</data>
      <data key="d6">system organ, immune filtration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="T-cell ALL" target="Thymus">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">T-cell ALL involves the thymus, where T-cell lymphoblasts proliferate, leading to th(is) enlargement and potential respiratory complications.&lt;SEP&gt;T-cell ALL involves the thymus, where T-cell lymphoblasts proliferate, leading to thymus enlargement and potential respiratory complications.</data>
      <data key="d6">organ involvement, disease progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymphatic system" target="Thymus">
