    </edge>
    <edge source="Ovarian Cancer" target="Ultrasound">
      <data key="d4">36.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Ultrasound is a primary imaging test used to visualize ovarian tumors, their size, and whether they are solid or fluid-filled.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultrasound is the first-line imaging test for ovarian cancer, providing initial visual data to assess abnormalities in the pelvic region and guide further diagnostic steps.</data>
      <data key="d6">imaging diagnosis, tumor characterization&lt;SEP&gt;initial diagnosis, imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Biopsy Procedure" target="Ultrasound">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Ultrasound imaging is used to visualize the prostate and guide the insertion of the biopsy needle during the procedure.</data>
