      <data key="d5">Genetic and Biomarker Tests are used to identify specific mutations or biomarkers in leukemia patients, aiding in treatment planning and prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic profiling, treatment targeting</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hormone Receptor Status" target="Immunohistochemistry (IHC)">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Immunohistochemistry (IHC) is used to detect hormone receptors in breast cancer cells, aiding in hormone receptor status classification.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic tool, molecular analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Karyotype" target="Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Karyotype analysis is a mutation testing method used to detect large-scale chromosomal abnormalities in AML, such as deletions or translocations.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal analysis, structural abnormalities</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FISH" target="Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FISH is a mutation testing technique that uses DNA probes to identify specific chromosomal abnormalities in AML cells that are too small to detect with other methods.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal detection, molecular analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NGS" target="Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NGS provides comprehensive mutation testing by sequencing the entire genome of AML cells to identify all genetic changes, enabling precise molecular profiling.</data>
      <data key="d6">genomic analysis, mutation detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PCR" target="Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PCR is a mutation testing method that amplifies specific DNA sequences to detect targeted genetic mutations in AML cells, supporting diagnosis and monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d6">targeted analysis, mutation detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Changes" target="Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mutation testing is a method used to detect and analyze genetic changes in leukemia cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic diagnosis, mutation detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genomic Testing" target="Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Genomic Testing and Mutation Testing are related, with Mutation Testing focusing on specific genetic alterations identified through broader genomic analysis.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic analysis, molecular profiling</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Testing Methods" target="Karyotype">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Karyotype analysis is a foundational genetic testing method that provides a visual representation of chromosomes, identifying structural abnormalities in leukemia cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal analysis, diagnostic imaging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLL" target="Karyotype">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Karyotype analysis detects chromosome defects in CLL, such as complex karyotypes, which may influence treatment strategies and prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosome analysis, genetic risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Testing Methods" target="Leukemia Predisposition Syndromes">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Genetic testing methods are used to identify inherited genetic mutations associated with leukemia predisposition syndromes, such as through skin biopsies or DNA analysis of unaffected tissues.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic testing, genetic inheritance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging Tests" target="Leukemia Predisposition Syndromes">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests are used to detect leukemia spread beyond bone marrow, complementing genetic testing in assessing the extent of the disease and treatment response.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease staging, diagnostic complement</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Polymerase Chain Reaction" target="Next-Generation Sequencing">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NGS relies on PCR products to analyze DNA mutations in greater detail.</data>
      <data key="d6">technological integration, genetic testing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging Tests" target="Brain CT Scan">
      <data key="d4">32.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A brain CT scan is a specific type of imaging test used to detect intracranial bleeding or other brain abnormalities associated with leukemia, often employing contrast material for improved visualization.&lt;SEP&gt;Brain CT scans are a type of imaging test used to detect intracranial abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic application, medical imaging&lt;SEP&gt;neuroimaging, contrast use</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging Tests" target="Brain MRI Scan">
      <data key="d4">32.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A brain MRI scan is another specific imaging test used to detect brain swelling from leukemia, offering non-radiation-based visualization of neurological involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Brain MRI scans are a type of imaging test used to detect brain inflammation or swelling.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic application, medical imaging&lt;SEP&gt;non-radiation imaging, neurological assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Lumbar Puncture">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lumbar puncture collects cerebroso spinal fluid to detect cancer cells, aiding in diagnosis and monitoring for CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Lumbar puncture collects cerebrospinal fluid to detect cancer cells, aiding in diagnosis and monitoring for CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">fluid analysis, diagnostic testing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Systemic Therapy" target="Medical Oncologist">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The medical oncologist oversees systemic therapy, which includes chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy for AML treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The medical oncologist oversees systemic therapy, which includes chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy for AML treatment.")</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment planning, systemic care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
