    <edge source="Biopsy" target="Pathologist">
      <data key="d4">74.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biopsy samples are examined by a pathologist to confirm cancer diagnosis and assess tumor characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologists analyze biopsy samples under a microscope to identify cancerous cells and determine disease characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologists analyze biopsy samples under a microscope to identify cancerous cells and determine the nature of the disease.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pathologist analyzes biopsy samples to confirm the presence of cancerous cells and determine tumor characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;The pathologist analyzes tissue samples obtained during biopsies to confirm cancer presence and determine tumor histology.&lt;SEP&gt;The pathologist examines biopsy samples to confirm cancer diagnosis and determine its characteristics and grade.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic analysis, cellular examination&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic analysis, pathological examination&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic analysis, tissue evaluation&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic confirmation, pathological analysis&lt;SEP&gt;tissue analysis, cancer diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </edge>
