    <edge source="Cystoscopy" target="Pathologist">
      <data key="d4">19.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Pathologist analyzes biopsy samples and urine cytology results obtained during Cystoscopy to confirm cancer diagnoses and guide treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pathologist examines biopsy samples and urine cytology results obtained during Cystoscopy to confirm the presence of cancer cells and determine treatment plans.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic analysis, procedural integration&lt;SEP&gt;procedural analysis, diagnostic confirmation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Urothelial Cancer" target="Pathologist">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The pathologist evaluates cancer cells to determine the grade and subtype of urothelial cancer, linking their expertise to cancer diagnosis and classification.</data>
