      <data key="d5">HPV infection is the primary cause of cervical cancer, with persistent infection leading to cellular changes.&lt;SEP&gt;HPV is the primary cause of cervical cancer, prompting combined screening methods like HPV/Pap co-tests.&lt;SEP&gt;HPV is the primary cause of cervical cancer, requiring screening methods to detect early changes.</data>
