      <data key="d6">cell type differentiation, diagnostic requirement</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="Fertility preservation">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NCCN provides guidelines and resources for fertility preservation in cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical guidelines, reproductive care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility specialist" target="Fertility preservation">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A fertility specialist guides patients in preserving fertility through methods like sperm or egg freezing before cancer treatment begins.</data>
      <data key="d6">fertility options, reproductive health</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility counselor" target="Fertility preservation">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A fertility counselor provides guidance and support for patients considering fertility preservation options during cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">reproductive planning, patient counseling</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Bone Marrow Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow biopsy checks for cancer cell presence, though rare in primary CNS lymphoma, to rule out bone involvement.</data>
      <data key="d6">tissue sampling, staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL)" target="Bone Marrow Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow biopsy confirms CLL by detecting abnormal cell proliferation in marrow samples.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic confirmation, tissue analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Process" target="Bone Marrow Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow biopsy is a critical diagnostic step for confirming CLL and assessing marrow involvement.</data>
      <data key="d6">procedural component, tissue analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Tools" target="Bone Marrow Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow biopsy is a diagnostic tool for confirming CLL and assessing marrow involvement.</data>
      <data key="d6">tissue analysis, diagnostic confirmation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Criteria" target="Bone Marrow Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone marrow biopsy results are part of diagnostic criteria for confirming CLL.</data>
      <data key="d6">tissue analysis, diagnostic confirmation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Translocation" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Translocation is a type of genetic change involving chromosomal segment exchange.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal abnormality, genetic mutation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Point Mutation" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Point mutation is a specific type of genetic change involving single nucleotide alteration.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic mutation, DNA alteration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Deletion" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Deletion is a genetic change characterized by missing DNA or chromosomal segments.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic deletion, chromosomal abnormality</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Insertion" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Insertion is a genetic change involving added DNA segments.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic insertion, chromosomal abnormality</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Inversion" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Inversion is a genetic change where chromosomal segments are reversed.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal inversion, genetic mutation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Amplification" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Amplification is a genetic change involving duplicated DNA segments.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic amplification, chromosomal abnormality</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gene Rearrangement" target="Genetic Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Gene rearrangement is a genetic change involving reordered DNA segments.</data>
      <data key="d6">chromosomal rearrangement, genetic mutation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Testing Methods" target="AML Mutation Testing">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AML mutation testing is a subset of genetic testing methods focused on detecting specific chromosomal and genetic abnormalities unique to acute myeloid leukemia (AML) cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">subcategory, diagnostic specialization</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FISH" target="Genetic Testing Methods">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FISH is a specific technique within genetic testing methods used to detect known chromosomal abnormalities in leukemia cells, particularly in blood or bone marrow samples.</data>
      <data key="d6">technique, chromosomal analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NGS" target="Genetic Testing Methods">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NGS represents an advanced genetic testing method that offers detailed DNA sequence analysis, surpassing traditional methods in detecting subtle mutations in leukemia-related genes.</data>
      <data key="d6">high-resolution sequencing, mutation detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PCR" target="Genetic Testing Methods">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PCR is a sensitive genetic testing method that amplifies DNA to detect minute genetic abnormalities, supporting NGS and treatment response monitoring in leukemia management.</data>
      <data key="d6">amplification, sensitivity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Biomarker testing" target="FISH">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FISH is a method used within biomarker testing to detect genetic abnormalities in cancer cells using fluorescent probes.</data>
      <data key="d6">testing methods, genetic analysis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLL" target="FISH">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FISH is a diagnostic category used to identify genetic abnormalities in CLL cells, such as the 17p deletion, which informs treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic testing, biomarker detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Biomarker testing" target="PCR">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PCR is a foundational technique in biomarker testing, amplifying DNA to generate samples for further genetic analysis.</data>
      <data key="d6">testing methods, DNA amplification</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="Cytarabine">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The NCCN provides guidelines on the use of cytarabine as an alternative chemotherapy option for primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">guideline provision, chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemotherapy" target="Methotrexate">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug commonly used in high doses to treat Primary CNS Lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">drug therapy, treatment method</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemotherapy" target="Multidisciplinary Team (MDT)">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The MDT is involved in selecting and overseeing chemotherapy protocols for AML patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment coordination, multidisciplinary care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Systemic Therapy" target="Multidisciplinary Team (MDT)">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The MDT integrates systemic therapy into personalized AML treatment plans.</data>
      <data key="d6">comprehensive care, treatment integration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Azacitidine (Vidaza)" target="Hypomethylating Agents (HMAs)">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Azacitidine is a specific drug classified under hypomethylating agents, which work by inhibiting DNA methylation to reactivate silenced genes.</data>
      <data key="d6">drug class, therapeutic mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Decitabine (Dacogen)" target="Hypomethylating Agents (HMAs)">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Decitabine is another drug classified under hypomethylating agents, which inhibit DNA methylation to restore gene expression in leukemic cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">drug class, therapeutic mechanism</data>
