    <edge source="Targeted Therapy" target="Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin (GO)">
      <data key="d4">36.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Gemtuzumab ozogamicin is a specific example of targeted therapy, which uses a chemotherapy drug linked to a monoclonal antibody targeting CD33 proteins on leukemic blasts.&lt;SEP&gt;Gemtuzumab ozogamicin is a targeted therapy that specifically binds to CD33 proteins on leukemic blasts, delivering chemotherapy directly to cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">therapeutic approach, drug specificity&lt;SEP&gt;treatment type, drug classification</data>
