      <data key="d7">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Semen" target="Seminal Vesicles">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Seminal Vesicles contribute to the composition of Semen, which is essential for fertility and reproductive processes.</data>
      <data key="d6">fluid composition, reproductive function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Breast Cancer Screening" target="Health Care Providers">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Health Care Providers are involved in Breast Cancer Screening, including specialists and radiologists who interpret test results and manage patient care.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical expertise, diagnostic collaboration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary Care Physician" target="Health Care Providers">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Primary Care Physician is a type of Health Care Provider who coordinates overall patient care, including breast cancer screening and follow-up.</data>
      <data key="d6">care coordination, patient management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PSA test" target="prostate cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The PSA test is a diagnostic method used to detect and monitor prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic methods, cancer detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="digital rectal exam" target="prostate cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The digital rectal exam is a physical examination used to detect abnormalities in the prostate gland, often in conjunction with the PSA test.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic methods, physical examination</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="active surveillance" target="prostate cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Active surveillance is a management strategy for early-stage prostate cancer to avoid unnecessary treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment options, patient management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="hormone therapy" target="prostate cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hormone therapy is a treatment modality for advanced-stage prostate cancer to suppress testosterone production.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer treatment, hormonal regulation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="surgery" target="prostate cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is a curative approach for localized prostate cancer, involving the removal of the prostate gland.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical intervention, cancer removal</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="digital rectal exam" target="PSA test">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Both the PSA test and digital rectal exam are commonly used diagnostic methods for prostate cancer, often performed together to assess the risk of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The PSA test and digital rectal exam are complementary diagnostic methods for prostate cancer screening.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer screening, diagnostic pairing&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic methods, cancer screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="localized prostate cancer" target="active surveillance">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Active surveillance is a monitoring strategy specifically suited for localized prostate cancer with low growth potential.</data>
      <data key="d6">early-stage management, non-invasive monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="early-stage prostate cancer" target="active surveillance">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Active surveillance is a standard approach for early-stage prostate cancer to delay or avoid immediate treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">early detection, conservative management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="metastatic prostate cancer" target="hormone therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hormone therapy is critical for managing metastatic prostate cancer by reducing testosterone-driven tumor growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">advanced-stage treatment, hormonal suppression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="early-stage cancer" target="surgery">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Early-stage cancer is typically treated with surgery, such as hysterectomy or trachelectomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Early-stage cancer is typically treated with surgery, which removes the uterus (hysterectomy) or allows fertility-sparing options.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment, surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stage 1A1" target="surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery, including radical trachelectomy, is a treatment option for Stage 1A1 cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood and Urine Tests" target="PSA Testing">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood and Urine Tests are used in conjunction with PSA Testing to refine cancer risk assessment and reduce false positives.</data>
      <data key="d6">complementary testing, risk stratification</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Digital Rectal Exam" target="PSA Testing">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PSA Testing and Digital Rectal Exam are complementary tests used together to assess prostate health and cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">combined screening, dual assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Treatment Team" target="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Treatment Team uses Digital Rectal Exam findings to assess the extent of Prostate Cancer and guide treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical assessment, staging evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Best Practices" target="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Best Practices include the use of Digital Rectal Exams as part of a comprehensive diagnostic approach for Prostate Cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital Rectal Exam is a recommended diagnostic procedure in Best Practices for assessing Prostate Cancer and guiding treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical examination, physical diagnosis&lt;SEP&gt;clinical standardization, physical diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PSA Test" target="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PSA Test results are often interpreted alongside findings from a Digital Rectal Exam to assess Prostate Cancer risk and progression.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic integration, physical assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Resolution Anoscopy" target="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Both procedures are diagnostic tools for anal cancer, with High-Resolution Anoscopy offering more detailed analysis than the Digital Rectal Exam.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic methods, medical procedures</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Anal Cancer" target="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Digital Rectal Exam is a standard initial procedure for detecting anal cancer, identifying abnormalities in the anal canal.</data>
      <data key="d6">early detection, diagnostic screening</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lymph Node Exam" target="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Digital rectal exams are part of the lymph node exam process to assess rectal abnormalities and lymph node involvement.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnostic Tests" target="Blood and Urine Tests">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood and Urine Tests are integral to Diagnostic Tests for confirming prostate cancer and guiding further interventions.</data>
      <data key="d6">biomarker integration, diagnostic refinement</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </edge>
