    <edge source="Androgen Deprivation Therapy (ADT)" target="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d4">36.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) is a specialized form of hormone therapy that directly reduces testosterone to combat prostate cancer."|&gt;"treatment subcategory, medical specialization&lt;SEP&gt;Androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) is a specialized form of hormone therapy that specifically targets and reduces testosterone to inhibit cancer growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">9&lt;SEP&gt;treatment specialization, hormone suppression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Surgical Castration" target="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgical castration is a permanent method of hormone therapy that eliminates testosterone production by removing the testicles.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment modality, hormone elimination</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LHRH Agonists" target="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">LHRH agonists are a class of medications used in hormone therapy to suppress testosterone production, preventing cancer cell proliferation.</data>
      <data key="d6">pharmacological treatment, hormone suppression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LHRH Antagonists" target="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">LHRH antagonists are medications used in hormone therapy to directly block testosterone production, reducing cancer growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">pharmacological treatment, hormone suppression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </edge>
