    <edge source="Prognostic stage" target="TNM system">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The TNM system forms the foundation of prognostic staging, which adds tumor grade and biomarker data to refine cancer prognosis and treatment planning.&lt;SEP&gt;The TNM system is a core component of the prognostic stage, which combines TNM data with tumor grade and biomarker status to predict outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d6">staging integration, prognostic factors&lt;SEP&gt;staging system, prognostic factors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pathologic stage" target="TNM system">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The TNM system underpins pathologic staging, which is validated through post-surgical tissue analysis to provide precise tumor and lymph node details.&lt;SEP&gt;The TNM system underpins the pathologic stage, which is determined through surgical examination of tissue to assess cancer extent and lymph node involvement.</data>
      <data key="d6">pathological assessment, surgical staging&lt;SEP&gt;pathological validation, surgical staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Clinical staging" target="TNM system">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The TNM system is used in clinical staging to evaluate cancer extent before treatment, based on physical exams, biopsies, and imaging without surgical intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;The TNM system is utilized in clinical staging to estimate cancer extent pre-treatment via non-invasive methods like imaging and biopsies.</data>
