      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Myeloid growth factors are used to counteract the side effects of chemotherapy, such as reduced white blood cell counts.&lt;SEP&gt;Myeloid growth factors are used to manage the side effects of chemotherapy, particularly to increase white blood cell counts and prevent infections.</data>
