    </edge>
    <edge source="High-dose Chemotherapy" target="Stem Cell Rescue">
      <data key="d4">29.0</data>
      <data key="d5">High-dose Chemotherapy is a prerequisite for Stem Cell Rescue, as it destroys both cancer cells and bone marrow stem cells, requiring the infusion of stored stem cells to regenerate blood cell production.&lt;SEP&gt;Stem Cell Rescue is initiated after High-dose Chemotherapy, which destroys both cancer cells and bone marrow stem cells, necessitating stem cell replacement to restore blood cell production.&lt;SEP&gt;Stem Cell Rescue is initiated after High-dose Chemotherapy, which destroys both cancer cells and bone marrow stem cells, necessitating stem cell replacement.</data>
      <data key="d6">bone marrow recovery, treatment sequence&lt;SEP&gt;chemotherapy recovery, stem cell regeneration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Rituximab (Rituxan)" target="Stem Cell Rescue">
