    <edge source="Hernia" target="Colectomy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hernia is a condition where organs or tissues push through weakened muscles or tissues, often a complication of surgical procedures like colectomy.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical complications, post-operative risks</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cancer Staging" target="American Joint Committee on Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The AJCC's TNM System is integral to cancer staging, providing a framework to describe tumor extent, lymph node status, and metastasis for treatment planning.&lt;SEP&gt;The AJCC's staging system is integral to determining cancer stages, which guide treatment and prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical staging, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stage 0a" target="Stage 0">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Stage 0a is a specific subcategory of Stage 0, describing cancer growth toward the bladder's hollow center.</data>
      <data key="d6">subclassification, cancer growth</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stage 0is" target="Stage 0">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Stage 0is (CIS) is a distinct subcategory of Stage 0, indicating flat, fast-growing cancer cells on the bladder lining.</data>
      <data key="d6">subclassification, aggressive cancer</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder Cancer" target="Stage 0">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Stage 0 represents the earliest non-invasive stage of bladder cancer, characterized by abnormal cells confined to the bladder lining.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer staging, non-invasive state</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemotherapy" target="Stage 1">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy is a recommended treatment for ovarian cancer, particularly for Stage 1 tumors, following surgical resection.</data>
