    <edge source="Brachytherapy" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Brachytherapy is used as an adjunct to EBRT for localized radiation therapy in early-stage cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is used as an adjunct to external beam radiation therapy for treating cervical cancer, particularly in early stages.</data>
      <data key="d6">radiation therapy, localized treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Extrafascial Hysterectomy" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Extrafascial hysterectomy is a surgical option for early-stage cervical cancer with specific criteria, such as no lymphovascular space invasion (LVSI).&lt;SEP&gt;Extrafascial hysterectomy is recommended for early-stage cervical cancer without LVSI or high-risk features.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical intervention, staging criteria</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Modified Radical Hysterectomy" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Modified radical hysterectomy is indicated for cancers with LVSI, larger tumor size, or high-risk features.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified radical hysterectomy is recommended for cancers that meet certain risk criteria, including LVSI and larger tumor size.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical staging, advanced treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Radical Hysterectomy" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radical hysterectomy is a definitive treatment for locally advanced cervical cancer, often combined with pelvic lymph node dissection.&lt;SEP&gt;Radical hysterectomy is the definitive surgical treatment for locally advanced cervical cancer, often combined with lymph node dissection.</data>
      <data key="d6">aggressive treatment, lymph node evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Para-aortic Lymph Node Dissection" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Para-aortic lymph node dissection is conducted for cancers that have spread beyond the pelvis, ensuring comprehensive lymph node evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Para-aortic lymph node dissection is conducted for cancers with pelvic or abdominal lymph node involvement, ensuring comprehensive staging.</data>
      <data key="d6">lymph node spread, advanced staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pelvic Lymph Node Dissection" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Pelvic lymph node dissection is performed to assess cancer spread and guide treatment decisions for advanced stages.</data>
      <data key="d6">lymph node assessment, staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT)" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">EBRT is a key component of chemoradiation for locally advanced cervical cancer, targeting pelvic tissues.</data>
      <data key="d6">radiation therapy, treatment integration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vaginal Brachytherapy" target="Cervical Cancer">
