    </edge>
    <edge source="Radical cystectomy" target="Bladder cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radical cystectomy is a primary treatment for muscle-invasive bladder cancer, involving the removal of the bladder and surrounding tissues.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment, surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Intravesical therapy" target="Bladder cancer">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Intravesical therapy is used to treat bladder cancer by delivering chemotherapy directly into the bladder to target malignant cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">chemotherapy, localized treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemotherapy" target="Bladder cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy is a systemic treatment for bladder cancer, often used in combination with other therapies to manage cancer progression.</data>
      <data key="d6">systemic treatment, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Diagnosis and treatment planning" target="Bladder cancer">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Diagnosis and treatment planning are essential steps in managing bladder cancer, involving assessment and personalized therapeutic strategies.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical process, oncology</data>
