    <edge source="Systemic Therapy" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">122.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy is a form of systemic therapy that affects the entire body.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a form of systemic therapy that uses drugs to kill cancer cells throughout the body, commonly used for cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a key component of systemic therapy, involving drugs that circulate through the bloodstream to target cancer cells throughout the body, often used alongside radiation for systemic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a specific type of systemic therapy that uses drugs to kill cancer cells, often administered as part of a broader systemic therapy regimen for advanced or metastatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a subset of systemic therapy, used alone or in combination with other treatments to address AML across the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a subset of systemic therapy, used alone or in combination with other treatments to address AML across the body.")&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy used to target cancer cells throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Therapy encompasses Chemotherapy, a treatment using drugs to kill cancer cells."|&gt;"includes&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic therapy includes chemotherapy, which is used in systemic treatment approaches for anal cancer to target cancer cells throughout the body.</data>
      <data key="d6">9&lt;SEP&gt;drug-based treatment, systemic approach&lt;SEP&gt;drug-based treatment, systemic impact&lt;SEP&gt;systemic treatment, drug therapy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment classification, systemic approach&lt;SEP&gt;treatment modality, chemotherapy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment modality, systemic approach&lt;SEP&gt;treatment modality, systemic effect</data>
